`/tmp/b8-ballot.txt`:
```
BALLOT B8 - read-only, vote independently, modify nothing.
Context: branch feat/wg-keepalive-relay, worktree ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive. The gateway's nginx gets a small http server relaying only the Pritunl WireGuard client keepalive (PUT /key/wg/..., about one per peer every 30 s) to Pritunl on 127.0.0.1:9700.
Question: upstream read timeout of that location.
Option 1: proxy_read_timeout 5s.
Option 2: no directive - nginx default 60 s, as in every other location of the role.
Read the template and spec first. Answer exactly:
B8 VOTE: <1|2>
REASON: <max five lines>
CONDITIONS: <conditions or none>
Reply in English.
```

**2. Bash, foreground** (seconds)
